# Walkthrough - gRPC HTTP Gateway & Postman Integration

We have successfully implemented the **gRPC HTTP Gateway reverse-proxy** for your inventory service. You can now make standard REST HTTP requests from **Postman**, web browsers, or any HTTP client, and the Gateway will translate them into gRPC calls sent to the Python backend server.

---

## 🛠️ Summary of Changes Made

### 1. Protocol Buffers (`proto/`)
- [inventory.proto](file:///d:/B.Tech%201st%20year/Sem-7/MAP/GRPC/proto/inventory.proto): Added Google API HTTP annotations (`option (google.api.http)`) mapping REST URLs to gRPC RPC methods.
- [annotations.proto](file:///d:/B.Tech%201st%20year/Sem-7/MAP/GRPC/proto/google/api/annotations.proto) & [http.proto](file:///d:/B.Tech%201st%20year/Sem-7/MAP/GRPC/proto/google/api/http.proto): Created Google API descriptor files for resolving HTTP option annotations.

### 2. Python Backend (`server-python/`)
- Updated protoc compilation command to generate `google/api/` stub dependencies alongside [inventory_pb2.py](file:///d:/B.Tech%201st%20year/Sem-7/MAP/GRPC/server-python/inventory_pb2.py).
- Improved error handling in [server.py](file:///d:/B.Tech%201st%20year/Sem-7/MAP/GRPC/server-python/server.py).

### 3. Node.js HTTP Gateway (`gateway-node/`)
- Created [gateway.js](file:///d:/B.Tech%201st%20year/Sem-7/MAP/GRPC/gateway-node/gateway.js): An Express-based reverse proxy running on `http://localhost:8080`.
- Receives HTTP REST requests from clients (Postman/Browser) and translates them into binary gRPC calls to the Python backend (`localhost:50053`).

